{"text": "Original Message \u2014\nFrom: McGamiek, Grendan J\nSent Friday, February 01, 2002 4:20 PM\nTor Mero, Elen; Culoy, a: Pe Michael E\nGe: Calahan, Stove: Mica, Vicnale\nSubject Brat Ft messages\n\nAttached are draft messages for use if PM USA gets calls regarding next week's press event\nannouncing the committee formation in FL. Please review and let me know if you have any\ncomments,\n\nDRAFT FOR DISCUSSION\nMESSAGES:\n\nPhilip Morris will join members of Florida's hospitality industry and business community in\nSupporting the Committee for Reasonable Solutions\u2019 efforts to provide voters with a reasonable\nalternative to the virtual smoking ban on the November ballot. We are supporting this elfort because\nWe support reasonable restrictions on smoking in publie places and believe that business owners\nshould continue to maintein some flexibility in making decisions about smoking in their\nestablishments.\n\nWe do not believe that amending the constitution to incorporate language related to public place\nfimoking isthe best way to address this issue, However, because proponents ofa virtual smoking\nban are moving ahead to place such a proposal on the ballot, we have decided to support the\nCommittee for Reasonable Solutions\u2019 effort to provide voters with a choice through a more\nreasonable initiative on the ballot.\n\nPOTENTIAL QUESTIONS:\n\nQ. How much will you spend?\nA. We anticipate that we will provide both financial and in-kind support to the committee. This\nSupport will be provided and reported in accordance with Florida law. We will not provide funding\nestimates outside of that process.\n\naS6ZE8LS807", "words": [{"text": "Original", "x0": 113, "y0": 103, "x1": 160, "y1": 113, "conf": 54.0}, {"text": "Message", "x0": 163, "y0": 104, "x1": 216, "y1": 114, "conf": 12.0}, {"text": "\u2014", "x0": 204, "y0": 93, "x1": 219, "y1": 121, "conf": 12.0}, {"text": "From:", "x0": 112, "y0": 102, "x1": 138, "y1": 130, "conf": 67.0}, {"text": "McGamiek